<title>ITALY: FORECAST-Italy seen issuing 11 trln lire BOTs.</title>
<headline>FORECAST-Italy seen issuing 11 trln lire BOTs.</headline>
<dateline>MILAN 1997-05-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Italian Treasury is seen issuing 10 to 12 trillion lire of short-term bills (BOT) at its next mid-month auction, for an average forecast of 11 trillion lire against 13 trillion maturing, analysts said.</p>
<p>The Treasury will detail the amount it will offer on Wednesday and the auction will be held on May 12. Settlement for the bills is on May 15.</p>
<p>The Treasury is also seen offering 4.5 trillion lire of 18 and 24 month zero coupon certificates (CTZ).</p>
<p>Following are the analysts' forecasts (in trln of lire):</p>
<p>		   3MoBot  6MoBot 12MoBot Tot Bot  18MoCtz   24MoCtz</p>
<p>Maturing	    3.0     5.0     5.0    13.0	 -	  -</p>
<p>	    ------------------------------------------------------</p>
<p>BCI		   3.0	4.5	4.5     12.0   2.0	2.5</p>
<p>Prometeia	   2.5	4.0	4.0     10.5	 8.0*</p>
<p>Chase Manhattan   3.0	4.0	4.0     11.0   2.0	2.5</p>
<p>Caboto		2.5	4.5	4.0     11.0   2.0	2.5</p>
<p>Bank of America   2.5	4.0	3.5     10.0   2.0	2.5</p>
<p>Credito Italiano  3.0	4.5	4.0     11.5   2.0	2.5</p>
<p>	    -----------------------------------------------------</p>
<p>CONSENSUS	   2.75     4.25     4.0     11.0   2.0	2.5</p>
<p>	    -----------------------------------------------------</p>
<p>* Prometeia's CTZ forecast is for the entire month of May.</p>
<p>-- Milan newsroom +392 66129437</p>
</text>
